{
  "id": "ticket_01KZ12QP04YSS8860GKR661F5P",
  "name": "Recover entity mutations missing audit events",
  "slug": "fix/audit-mutation-recovery",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Add a durable flatfile mutation journal so committed entity writes recover exactly one audit event after failure or crash.",
    "details_md": "Pre-mint event identity and persist an idempotent create/update/delete intent before changing an entity. Replay under the repository lock on storage open and transaction entry; complete from the recorded before state, accept the recorded after state, reject third-state conflicts, verify an existing event matches, and retire completed intents durably.",
    "acceptance": [
      "A committed ticket or session create/update is eventually paired with exactly one stable event after event-write failure or SIGKILL.",
      "Replaying a completed intent is harmless and never duplicates or overwrites a conflicting event.",
      "Create, update, and delete journal states have explicit before/after recovery behavior.",
      "Corrupt journals and entity/event conflicts fail loudly without modifying entity or event data.",
      "Storage open and transaction entry recover pending intents while holding the repository lock."
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/repo/events.ts",
      "src/repo/mutation-journal.ts",
      "src/storage/flatfile.ts",
      "src/storage/open.ts"
    ],
